description:
Hello, our name is Customertimes, but you can call us CT. We are a global digital engineering, product development, and technology consulting company. Headquartered in New York, we have a team of 1000+ experts working across 65+ countries.
About this job:
Data Engineer / Data Readiness Analyst (2 seats, Middle level) for our client, one of the largest specialty provider networks in the US and part of a major healthcare company. The network includes independent and affiliated practices in urology, gastroenterology, rheumatology, and oncology. The goal is to turn practice EHR data (joined with pathology and genomic reports, medical claims, and disease registries at the patient level) into real-world data products that pharma and biotech companies license and build on, starting with prostate and bladder cancer.
These are two people who build and check the data. One leans toward building pipelines; the other leans toward measuring the data and showing it is ready to sell. Both work hands-on in SQL and the data every day.
• Start: As soon as possible;
• Length: 6-month initial term, expected to extend well past that;
• Hours: Full-time, US Eastern business hours;
• Team mix: Each seat can be supported by, or blended with, nearshore or offshore staff;
• Data platform: Databricks (Delta Lake, medallion architecture) on Azure, alongside a large SQL Server estate with legacy stored procedures.
Location: Remote, on-site not required; nearshore or onshore
How you'll make an impact:
• Build pipelines that load practice EHR, pathology, and claims data into the data model;
• Standardize messy clinical data: codes, dates, units, and free text;
• Measure fill rates and coverage by source, practice, and disease;
• Rerun the same count and get the same answer on every refresh;
• Flag what changed between refreshes, and why;
• Find and fix broken or late feeds before customers notice;
• Document what was built: mappings, rules, and the data dictionary;
• Deliver files and extracts to customers on schedule.
What makes you a great fit:
Experience building pipelines or data quality checks on patient-level EHR or claims data;
• Strong SQL and data profiling skills, and experience building in Databricks with PySpark and Spark SQL;
Knowledge of clinical codes: ICD-10, CPT, NDC, and LOINC;
Knowledge of how EHR data differs across vendors and practices;
Ability to build from written specs and test the result against them.
You are a star if you have:
Experience working at a real-world data company or at a provider network that sells its data;
Experience with oncology or urology data;
Experience with Git and CI/CD using Azure DevOps or GitHub Actions;
Experience with T-SQL on SQL Server, including legacy stored procedures;
Knowledge of EHR exports, HL7 and FHIR basics, and the OMOP common data model;
Experience building data readiness or data quality scorecards;
Experience with patient matching and tokenization;
Ability to work well across time zones with US-based leads.
If you're looking to contribute to global projects, grow your skills, shape the way you work, and be part of a connected international community — Customertimes is the place to build your next career chapter. Are you ready to spark the tech with us?
